      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "content": "## HR Zone Anchors \u2014 Calculated from Data\n\nAll values below are **read from InfluxDB** (`PhysiologyDaily`). The stat panels above show the live values. The table to the right shows the actual zone boundaries in use.\n\n| Anchor | Live Value | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| **HRmax** | See stat panel | `PhysiologyDaily.HRmax_est` \u2014 from observed peak |\n| **RHR (7d median)** | See stat panel | `PhysiologyDaily.RHR_7d_median` \u2014 rolling |\n| **HRR** | See stat panel | `PhysiologyDaily.HRR` = HRmax \u2212 RHR |\n\n> \u26a0\ufe0f **Note on RHR baseline:** The pipeline uses a 7-day rolling median RHR, which shifts with training load and stress. Current RHR baseline is elevated vs the historical floor. This is real: elevated training load and/or less recovery.\n\n---\n\n### Zone Method \u2014 Karvonen (HRR-based)\nZones are calculated as: `RHR + (HRR \u00d7 %)`\n\n| Zone | Name | % HRR |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Z1** | Recovery | 50\u201360% |\n| **Z2** | Aerobic Base | 60\u201370% |\n| **Z3** | Aerobic Threshold | 70\u201380% |\n| **Z4** | Lactate Threshold | 80\u201390% |\n| **Z5** | VO2max | 90\u2013100% |\n\nActual BPM boundaries are live in the **Zone Boundaries** table to the right.\n\n---\n\n### HRmax Evidence\n\nPipeline uses **183 bpm** (observed 184 bpm on 5 Feb 2025). A **189 bpm** was recorded on 1 Jun 2026 (running, avgHR 165, 20 min). If genuine, the athlete profile should be updated. Trail running max = 180 (reliable, sustained).\n\n---\n\n### LTHR Status\n\u26a0\ufe0f `LTHR_run_bpm_est` is not currently being calculated (null in `PerformanceDaily`). The `lthr_used` values in `DerivedActivity` show 181\u2013186 bpm \u2014 near HRmax and physiologically implausible. Pipeline misconfiguration. Best proxy: 20-min HR from sustained efforts.\n\n---\n\n### Device\nCurrent device: **Instinct 3 - 50mm, AMOLED**\n\n**Medication note:** Atenolol + Vyvanse. Elevated RHR baseline (~60 bpm rolling) narrows HRR and shifts all zone boundaries upward.\n\n**Ultra target:** 80\u201385% of weekly volume in Z1\u2013Z2.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "targets": [],
      "title": "HR ZONES \u2014 Live from PhysiologyDaily (Karvonen / HRR-based)",
      "type": "text"
    },
